  "summary": "Embroidered quilts featuring intricate running stitch patterns and narrative designs.",
  "description": "Nakshi kantha quilts are created by layering old saris and dhotis with running stitch embroidery in intricate patterns of flowers, birds, and narrative scenes. These textiles serve as both practical bedding and storytelling canvases, with motifs often drawn from rural Bangladeshi life and mythology.",
